course: dictionary
lesson: 5439
title: Lamp in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lamp is a thing that gives light. You can find lamps on a table, on a desk, or along a street. When you read the word «lamp», look at the words around it, because they give you clues. «Turn on the lamp, it's getting dark» tells you a lamp is something you switch on to see better.
explain: Context can also show you what a lamp is made of, or how it works. «Old lamps burned oil or gas to make light» tells you that long ago people used oil or gas, and that most lamps today use electricity. The clue words are burned and make light.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning in different places. A «lamp post» is the tall post that holds a street lamp. A «heat lamp» is a lamp that gives warmth, not just light. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: A lamp is a thing that gives light.
fact: Old lamps burned oil or gas, and most lamps today use electricity.
fact: A heat lamp gives warmth as well as, or instead of, light.
fact: «Lamp post» means the post that holds a street lamp.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Turn on the lamp, it's getting dark.» What is a lamp? | A thing for cooking food | A kind of sweet | *A thing that gives light | A sort of bird
exercise: «Old lamps burned oil or gas to make light.» What did old lamps burn to make light? | Wood only | Sand | *Oil or gas | Water
exercise: «The street lamp glowed all night beside the lamp post.» Find and copy the word that names a thing that gives light. | *lamp | night | street | glowed
test: «A heat lamp gives warmth.» What does a heat lamp give? | Sound | Light only | Water | *Warmth
test: Which of these is a lamp? | A pencil case | A bicycle bell | *A street lamp | A sofa
exam: In «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated with lamps, sweets and fireworks», what are the lamps? | Fireworks | Sweets | People who celebrate | *Things that give light
